> recently.  My third question is: How ofen can I pray before my God says,
> "Enough already!  No more free stomach filling for you!" ?
> (ie, does Prayer stop working at any point?)

Prayer doesn't stop working, but rather has a timeout. Certain things
increase it, and turns passing and sacrificing decreases it. Off the
top of my head, praying, recieving a gift through sacrifice and wishing
for something all increase timeout. As does failed prayer? Crowned
characters get a longer timeout. Depending on how serious your problem
is, you can pray even when the timeout hasn't completely timed out
(something like 100 left for minor problems and 250 for serious
problems?). I *think* if you only pray while weak, you could keep it up
indefinitely (being weak IIRC is a major problem). However, you could
get unlucky with whatever it gets set to after praying, and of course,
this means you can't pray for anything else.

> Finally, what exactly does a Ring of Warning do?  I'm wearing one (I'm
> not sure where it came from.  I think I may've started with it.) and it
> doesn't seem to be warning me about anything.  This could be a good
> thing, actually.

When you have warning, within a certain range monsters you can't see
are represented by a number showing how much of a threat they are (1
being 'causing you concern' through to 5 being 'causing you dread').
Weak monsters do not show up on warning at all, which is likely the
case at your xlvl.

